Unreleased
----------
* Breaking: `revoke()` now clears `curr_async_result_id` and detaches the AsyncResult (returning `NOT_SCHEDULED`) after broadcasting the revoke, so a task stuck in `STARTED` after worker loss can be queued again
* Admin Revoke and Terminate actions are no longer limited to tasks present in the Redis queue; they are available for any scheduled task
* add Django 6.0 to the test matrix

